# Routh I.Art.167 Ex.1 — equal speeds in all directions give an expanding
# SPHERE — dynamic notebook
#
# E. J. Routh, "A Treatise on Dynamics of a Particle" (Cambridge, 1898),
# Part I, Art. 167, Ex. 1: "Particles are projected from a given point O at
# the same instant with equal velocities in different directions; prove that
# the locus at any time is a sphere."
#
# THE PROOF. Again Art. 154's independence principle. Each particle obeys
#
#     r_i(t) = O + V*n_i*t + (1/2)*g*t^2
#
# where n_i is its own unit direction and V the common speed. Subtract the
# part that does not depend on i:
#
#     r_i(t) - [ O + (1/2)*g*t^2 ]  =  V*t*n_i
#
# The left side has length V*t for EVERY particle, whatever n_i is. So at each
# instant the swarm lies exactly on a sphere of radius V*t, centred not at O
# but at the point O + (1/2)*g*t^2 -- the position of a particle dropped from
# rest at O. The sphere expands linearly in time while its centre falls.
#
# WHY IT IS PRETTY. The individual paths are parabolas of every shape: some
# almost vertical, some flat, some thrown downwards. Nothing about one path
# suggests a sphere. The sphere is a statement about the whole family at one
# instant, and it exists only because gravity adds the same vector to all of
# them.
#
# THE NUMBERS. V = 5, gravity (0, -9.81, 0), O the origin, six particles fired
# along +x, -x, +y, -y, +z, -z. The free-fall centre is at
#
#     C(t) = (0, -4.905*t^2, 0)
#
# so at t = 1 the sphere has centre (0, -4.905, 0) and radius 5, and at t = 2
# centre (0, -19.62, 0) and radius 10. The cells print each particle's distance
# from that centre: six identical numbers at each instant, including for the
# particle thrown straight down, which is moving fastest of all.
#
# SETUP NOTE. system.g_constant = 0 so the particles do not attract each other;
# the uniform field is the only force, which is exactly Routh's problem.
#
# WHAT YOU WATCH: a shell of particles blowing outward at constant rate while
# the whole shell falls -- a sphere whose centre is in free fall.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LAUNCH (run from the repository root: /Users/youruser/Developer/code/rust/rustSimulate)
#
#     posim_notebook routh_p1_expanding_sphere
#
# or, without the shell alias, the always-available form:
#
#     cargo run -p posim --release -- --notebook dynamic_notebooks/routh_p1_expanding_sphere.posim
#
# The scene window opens in your browser. To start the simulation, press Start
# in that window, or type this at the In[] prompt in the terminal:
#
#     scene start
#
# If no browser should be launched (the URL is printed instead), use:
#
#     POSIM_NO_BROWSER=1 cargo run -p posim --release -- --notebook dynamic_notebooks/routh_p1_expanding_sphere.posim
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

set system.g_constant = 0
set system.gravity = [0, -9.81, 0]
set system.rtol = 1e-13
set system.atol = 1e-15

new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 5, 0, 0] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [-5, 0, 0] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 0, 5, 0] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 0,-5, 0] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 0, 0, 5] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 0, 0,-5] }

run 1 steps 1
# radius 5 about the free-fall centre (0, -4.905, 0), for every particle
norm(obj0.position - [0, -4.905, 0])
norm(obj3.position - [0, -4.905, 0])
norm(obj4.position - [0, -4.905, 0])

run 1 steps 1
# radius 10 about (0, -19.62, 0)
norm(obj0.position - [0, -19.62, 0])
norm(obj3.position - [0, -19.62, 0])
norm(obj4.position - [0, -19.62, 0])
reset

set system.g_constant = 0
set system.gravity = [0, -9.81, 0]
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 5, 0, 0] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [-5, 0, 0] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 0, 5, 0] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 0,-5, 0] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 0, 0, 5] }
new point { mass = 1, position = [0,0,0], velocity = [ 0, 0,-5] }

scene create
scene set_time_step 0.02
